{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0390","billNumberShort":"H.B. 390","billNumberLong":"HB0390S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0855","shortTitle":"Veterans PTSD Clinical Research Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"DAILEJ","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Dailey-Provost, Jennifer","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"CULLIKA","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Cullimore, Kirk A.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses psychedelic-assisted therapy for certain veterans.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>authorizes the Huntsman Mental Health Institute (Huntsman) to conduct a clinical study on the safety and feasibility of psychedelic-assisted therapy for veterans with treatment-resistant post-traumatic stress disorder;<hr><ltbullet>permits Huntsman to accept donations to fund the clinical study;<hr><ltbullet>requires Huntsman to begin the clinical study if legislative appropriations and donations combined are equal to or exceed an amount sufficient to begin the study;<hr><ltbullet>requires reporting to the Health and Human Services Interim Committee; <hr><ltbullet>provides a sunset date for the provisions related to the clinical study;<hr><ltbullet>defines terms; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Amy Shewan","fiscalAnalyst":"Josh Pittman","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/19/2026","trackingID":"EAYXJQBAYX","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-26 16:25:52.217","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-26 16:25:52.217","actionC